{"lines":[{"h":0.01893443288832819,"w":0.1343922170003255,"c":1,"y":0.085624060235260591,"t":"READING","x":0.42505795059109858},{"h":0.015988371899566256,"c":1,"x":0.075728149564511488,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","y":0.15261627916130494,"w":0.30485438028971357},{"h":0.019003115264797588,"y":0.19034267916323899,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","x":0.075728159832351788,"w":0.81359222412109367,"c":1},{"h":0.016035463208350142,"x":0.075728155962631924,"w":0.16893203735351564,"c":1,"t":"Passage 1 below.","y":0.21075581403879662},{"c":1,"h":0.02476182741539501,"x":0.22135923082733427,"w":0.54563105265299483,"t":"Materials to take us beyond concrete","y":0.24704049871273748},{"h":0.021042761401595333,"x":0.08537920344508175,"c":1,"w":0.81759246826171861,"t":"Concrete is everywhere, but it's bad for the planet, generating large amounts of carbon","y":0.28906526869644433},{"w":0.39999999999999997,"h":0.017584945702478483,"c":1,"x":0.29320388340047338,"t":"dioxide - alternatives are being developed","y":0.31090342649675284},{"x":0.077669903286198494,"t":"B","w":0.013592232068379728,"h":0.014534883112922281,"y":0.5174418606237714,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.01453488311292217,"y":0.64825581415367184,"w":0.019417475064595541,"t":"C","x":0.075728155560628715},{"w":0.75742894490559898,"y":0.34722807990746118,"x":0.12032423210666707,"t":"Concrete is the second most used substance in the global economy, after water - and one","c":1,"h":0.020965029517438172},{"y":0.36561342356120752,"h":0.020570568429346792,"t":"of the world's biggest single sources of greenhouse gas emissions. The chemical process","w":0.75740921020507812,"x":0.11838731596382236,"c":1},{"t":"by which cement, the key ingredient of concrete, is created results in large quantities of","y":0.38326011366353319,"x":0.12029866555007743,"w":0.74777811686197915,"h":0.022340994386286672,"c":1},{"x":0.12038835622615475,"c":1,"y":0.40404984453001636,"t":"carbon dioxide. The UN estimates that there will be 9.8 billion people living on the planet","h":0.017461782675294413,"w":0.76893203735351556},{"t":"by mid-century. They will need somewhere to live. If concrete is the only answer to the","c":1,"x":0.12032766767664195,"w":0.74769378662109376,"y":0.42234719607413507,"h":0.020056797633661305},{"t":"construction of new cities, then carbon emissions will soar, aggravating global warming.","y":0.44174454850239053,"w":0.75533981323242183,"c":1,"x":0.12233009338651622,"h":0.019011265169422975},{"c":1,"x":0.122235886696632,"y":0.45914489837960271,"t":"And so scientists have started innovating with other materials, in a scramble for alternatives","h":0.021211193952233698,"w":0.78271662394205743},{"t":"to a universal commodity that has underpinned our modern life for many years.","x":0.12038835197239393,"y":0.47965116262201124,"w":0.6815533955891927,"h":0.017545099347551329,"c":1},{"x":0.12033468527460305,"t":"The problem with replacing concrete is that it is so very good at what it does.","w":0.66223765055338546,"h":0.018729294869015978,"y":0.51632003191547249,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Chris Cheeseman, an engineering professor at Imperial College London, says the key","w":0.72827987670898431,"x":0.12227462747735236,"y":0.53440273399201554,"h":0.02124870514201227},{"c":1,"w":0.76128168741861979,"t":"thing to consider is the extent to which concrete is used around the world, and is likely to","h":0.019872257197014576,"y":0.55291760527902989,"x":0.1203348035802559},{"t":"continue to be used. 'Concrete is not a high-carbon product. Cement is high carbon, but","y":0.57258566973741643,"h":0.017530609439837863,"c":1,"w":0.74757283528645835,"x":0.12233008714130506},{"c":1,"t":"concrete is not. But it is the scale on which it is used that makes it high carbon. The sheer","x":0.12233009158634578,"y":0.59156976753574408,"w":0.76116505940755208,"h":0.015988371899566256},{"x":0.12027917124460055,"h":0.021959405821803224,"t":"scale of manufacture is so huge, that is the issue.'","y":0.60872464586671371,"w":0.42746109008789057,"c":1},{"w":0.76516128540039063,"h":0.019466775674314873,"y":0.64613279091292941,"c":1,"x":0.11646113391109708,"t":"Not only are the ingredients of concrete relatively cheap and found in abundance in most"},{"c":1,"x":0.122189717051376,"w":0.74200520833333328,"t":"places around the globe, the stuff itself has marvellous properties: Portland cement, the","y":0.6634749106048029,"h":0.022143997952945527},{"y":0.68459302352878271,"t":"vital component of concrete, is mouldable and pourable, but quickly sets hard. Cheeseman","c":1,"x":0.12233010564631892,"h":0.018895348284474811,"w":0.77087376912434891},{"x":0.12233010092481085,"h":0.017591284517187278,"c":1,"w":0.78058252970377606,"y":0.70203488398654967,"t":"also notes another advantage: concrete and steel have similar thermal expansion properties,"},{"x":0.12225754887008861,"t":"so steel can be used to reinforce concrete, making it far stronger and more flexible as a","h":0.021589724817008604,"y":0.72071788854223262,"c":1,"w":0.73994766235351572},{"h":0.018895348284474811,"c":1,"y":0.73982558143552424,"w":0.74757278442382813,"t":"building material than it could be on its own. According to Cheeseman, all these factors","x":0.12233011116187242},{"t":"together make concrete hard to beat. 'Concrete is amazing stuff. Making anything with","x":0.12227056676316901,"h":0.021337452113071254,"w":0.74185770670572915,"y":0.75634216789070841,"c":1},{"x":0.12215380398281867,"t":"similar properties is going to be very difficult.'","h":0.021331965366256478,"w":0.40236445109049473,"y":0.77608938994705212,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.76126978556315095,"y":0.81431352447807748,"t":"A possible alternative to concrete is wood. Making buildings from wood may seem like a","x":0.12227862269493632,"h":0.018607269714925989},{"t":"rather medieval idea, but climate change is driving architects to turn to treated timber as","x":0.12031594335301349,"w":0.75354970296223955,"y":0.83259392713378833,"h":0.020571760373694903,"c":1},{"x":0.12223959342122243,"w":0.74388463338216138,"y":0.85148859090881801,"h":0.020078449902876105,"t":"a possible resource. Recent years have seen the emergence of tall buildings constructed","c":1},{"y":0.87196261694441246,"h":0.017572266884681942,"c":1,"x":0.12233009426742864,"t":"almost entirely from timber. Vancouver, Vienna and Brumunddal in Norway are all home to","w":0.78058252970377606},{"y":0.89096573195236461,"t":"constructed tall, wooden buildings.","h":0.019003115264797588,"w":0.30291262308756511,"c":1,"x":0.1223300961563253},{"h":0.014534883112922281,"c":1,"w":0.025242718060811353,"x":0.88543689318318641,"t":"61","y":0.9549418606237714}],"h":3209,"w":2400}